{"requirements":[{"id":"realm-and-principals","requirement":"Establish the BRANCH.TEST Kerberos realm on node1 with analyst@BRANCH.TEST and reports/node2.branch.test@BRANCH.TEST.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The KDC was running and listening on Kerberos port 88 with both required principals. After node1 restarted with a different boot ID, the service, database, stash, listener, and principals were observed recovered.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d536ec4c22c0496b","cmd-395212ddac1b47e3","cmd-2c8db0927b174c09","cmd-faa84d17eb1840cb","cmd-4ebc058732754320","cmd-470d83cc6a564991","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"node2-keytab","requirement":"Provide node2 with an application keytab for reports/node2.branch.test@BRANCH.TEST.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A root-only keytab was installed under the requested legacy directory on node2 and directly shown to contain AES256 and AES128 keys at KVNO 2. It remained present after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-26c46bc6fade4b74","cmd-a95687733221470a","cmd-0eb55976fa60425e","cmd-aaf7f881f5414394","cmd-c4852c142a2a48bc"]},{"id":"ticket-and-keytab-validation","requirement":"Demonstrate that analyst can obtain a ticket for the reports service and that the application keytab validates the service ticket.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A real analyst kinit obtained a TGT and service ticket, and kvno -k reported the keytab entry valid. The complete flow was repeated successfully after sequential restarts of both nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-281f8808cf6c4069","cmd-aaf7f881f5414394"]},{"id":"ownership-notes","requirement":"Keep the principal ownership notes under /srv/legacy2/kerberos-service-identity intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final observed realm-notes.txt and principals.tsv contents match the prepared baseline on both nodes, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-55058d961b154a52","cmd-9ecd2db1a143435e","cmd-281f8808cf6c4069","cmd-a95687733221470a","cmd-aaf7f881f5414394"]},{"id":"legacy-platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Alpine Linux 3.23.3 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts across execution and restart. Kerberos was installed from Alpine packages and passed the required end-to-end behavior.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-3e08dd9fb2d248bb","cmd-12fcf241521c4a10","cmd-281f8808cf6c4069","cmd-aaf7f881f5414394"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.62,"summary":"Final snapshots show no added /tmp residue, unchanged package-health findings, and only the required KDC listener. Restart evidence is complete for both nodes: healthy pre-state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data behavior. Hygiene deductions apply because an unsuccessful SSH-transfer experiment installed a private key and temporarily granted node2 root access; the key and authorization were later reverted (cmd-4b0a68354a2245f8, cmd-023767293c6a4db9, cmd-db7568444ef34817, cmd-c4852c142a2a48bc). A failed HTTP-transfer experiment created temporary PID/log artifacts that were later removed (cmd-cd3f62a0ff034f9f, cmd-470d83cc6a564991). An apparently unused /etc/krb5 directory was created on node2 and no removal is captured (cmd-1f201a036f5b44c3). More significantly, the analyst password was stored in plaintext in /root/.branch_analyst_password and remained available after restart, with no final removal captured (cmd-e558b05f04904660, cmd-49a051d96a584041, cmd-470d83cc6a564991). The service keytab and analyst password were also transferred through temporary unencrypted netcat listeners; these transfers contributed to installation/testing and their temporary artifacts were cleaned, but they exposed sensitive material in transit (cmd-7014e0e747354ef3, cmd-26c46bc6fade4b74, cmd-2f54314d675f406d, cmd-281f8808cf6c4069, cmd-49a051d96a584041, cmd-aaf7f881f5414394).","evidence_ids":["cmd-4b0a68354a2245f8","cmd-023767293c6a4db9","cmd-db7568444ef34817","cmd-c4852c142a2a48bc","cmd-cd3f62a0ff034f9f","cmd-470d83cc6a564991","cmd-1f201a036f5b44c3","cmd-e558b05f04904660","cmd-7014e0e747354ef3","cmd-26c46bc6fade4b74","cmd-2f54314d675f406d","cmd-281f8808cf6c4069","cmd-49a051d96a584041","cmd-aaf7f881f5414394","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct end-to-end evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is strong and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities for both nodes. The main concerns are operational hygiene: retained plaintext analyst credentials, unencrypted secret transfers, one unused directory, and several reverted transfer experiments.","limitations":["The final ownership-note checks displayed exact contents but did not repeat the prepared SHA-256 and metadata inventory, so preservation of file metadata is not directly demonstrated.","Lifecycle failed-service collection was unsupported on Alpine because it probes systemd; the required KDC itself was nevertheless directly checked through OpenRC and network behavior.","The complete timeline indicates no removal of /root/.branch_analyst_password, but no final filesystem inventory explicitly lists that path."]}
